And now I have actually looked at the source and seen it is as easy
thing to do as I thought.

The relevant change will be in the dofire() function in dothrow.c.
When the game shows the message that you have no ammunition readied, 
instead of calling dothrow() and returning, call dowieldquiver() and
continue with the rest of dofire() after the "if (!uquiver)" condition
block.

I tested that it works that way and added a binary option quiver_fired to
toggle the behavior on and off, and when I have updated the Guidebook with
the explanation of the additional option, I will extract a diff and
release it.

